NEARS-2223 QA — task_bug: AC3 ("the allowPending branch, when taken, produces
exactly ONE structured log line ... grep-verified in laravel.log") fails on the
GRANTED path in the real environment.

Code (Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Vendor/SubscriptionController.php,
authorizeStore):
    Log::{$ok ? 'info' : 'warning'}('subscription.allow_pending', ['store_id' => $store->id, 'outcome' => $ok ? 'granted' : 'denied']);

Both this worktree's Admin/.env and the primary tree's Admin/.env set
LOG_LEVEL=warning (confirmed identical, not a QA-environment artifact). Laravel's
minimum log level for the 'stack'/default channel is therefore 'warning' — any
Log::info(...) call is silently dropped before it reaches the Monolog handler,
never written to storage/logs/laravel.log.

=== Live proof ===
$ grep -n "^LOG_LEVEL" Admin/.env
LOG_LEVEL=warning

$ php artisan tinker --execute="Log::info('qa_test_info_marker_xyz', ['a'=>1]); Log::warning('qa_test_warning_marker_xyz', ['a'=>1]);"
$ grep -n "qa_test_info_marker_xyz\|qa_test_warning_marker_xyz" storage/logs/laravel.log
4081:[2026-08-19 09:25:51] production.WARNING: qa_test_warning_marker_xyz {"a":1}
(the info marker line is entirely absent — zero matches)

=== Consequence for AC3 ===
The one successful (granted) live business_plan call demonstrated in this QA run
(store 91114, commission path) produced ZERO matching log lines in laravel.log —
grep -n "91114" storage/logs/laravel.log returns nothing at all, not even a
"granted" line. Only the DENIED (Log::warning) path is observable in production/dev
logs, e.g.:
[2026-08-19 09:20:14] production.WARNING: subscription.allow_pending {"trace_id":"a391fc9c7a60651f88824b1ea60913c1","correlation_id":"30869d58-611d-42b1-be2f-039b05786a23","store_id":91114,"outcome":"denied"}
(this line is from the REPLAY call for the same store, which is correctly denied —
the earlier GRANT for the same store_id has no corresponding log line at all).

=== Why the pinned test missed it ===
Admin/tests/Feature/Security/RegistrationNonceTest.php::test_allow_pending_branch_logs_exactly_one_line_on_grant
uses Log::spy(), which intercepts calls at the Facade layer and asserts they were
CALLED — it never engages the real Monolog handler + LOG_LEVEL minimum-level
filter, so it cannot observe (and therefore cannot catch) an Log::info() call being
dropped by the actual environment's configured log level. The test is
green (confirmed: vendor/bin/phpunit --filter RegistrationNonceTest, 9/9) but does
not exercise the failure mode that exists in the real, deployed configuration.

Fix direction (not implemented by QA — reported for the engineer): either use
Log::warning() unconditionally for this line (matching the denied path, and the
existing otp-send/auth limiter logging convention elsewhere in this codebase), or
add a dedicated log channel/level for this line that survives LOG_LEVEL=warning.
